//! WIT text parsing migration anchor (`std::wit`, #044, #706, #917).
//!
//! The former `parse_full` / `parse_full_import_text` / `parse_wit` free
//! functions were retired by the #917 WIT parser wave (ADR-044/ADR-046).
//! Callers migrate to the canonical `std::wit::ast` surface:
//!
//! - `WitNode::parse(source)` for the full WIT 1.0 AST, including worlds.
//! - `WitNode::import_metadata(source)` for compiler-safe import metadata.
//!
//! The reduced `parse_wit` World-shaped compatibility parser retires with the
//! wave. A direct `World::parse` associated replacement is blocked on
//! wasm32-gc: returning `Result<World, error::Error>` from a std associated
//! function or method fails Wasm validation, so callers parse to `WitNode`
//! and build a `World` with the public builders instead.
//!
//! The module itself stays until the 1.0.0 era so qualified calls resolve to
//! an E0100 migration hint instead of an undefined-module error; delete it
//! once the removal window closes.
